# What Flatpak calls the things profiles ask for.
#
# Application ids are reverse-DNS, so this is a third vocabulary
# alongside dpkg and rpm rather than a third mechanism. It is loaded
# in addition to the ecosystem's own table, not instead of it, so a
# capability can be met from the base repositories or from Flatpak and
# both appear as options.

Capability: web-browser
Resolves-To: org.mozilla.firefox | com.google.Chrome | org.chromium.Chromium

Capability: word-processor
Resolves-To: org.libreoffice.LibreOffice | org.onlyoffice.desktopeditors

Capability: spreadsheet
Resolves-To: org.libreoffice.LibreOffice | org.onlyoffice.desktopeditors

Capability: image-viewer
Resolves-To: org.gnome.Loupe | org.kde.gwenview

Capability: image-editor
Resolves-To: org.gimp.GIMP | org.kde.krita | com.github.PhotoFlare.photoflare

Capability: video-editor
Resolves-To: org.kde.kdenlive | org.shotcut.Shotcut | fr.natron.Natron

Capability: video-player
Resolves-To: org.videolan.VLC | io.mpv.Mpv | org.gnome.Totem

Capability: audio-editor
Resolves-To: org.audacityteam.Audacity | org.ardour.Ardour

Capability: text-editor
Resolves-To: org.gnome.TextEditor | org.kde.kate | com.vscodium.codium

Capability: code-editor
Resolves-To: com.vscodium.codium | org.kde.kdevelop | com.jetbrains.CLion

Capability: chat-client
Resolves-To: com.discordapp.Discord | org.telegram.desktop | im.riot.Riot

Capability: steam
Resolves-To: com.valvesoftware.Steam

Capability: document-viewer
Resolves-To: org.gnome.Evince | org.kde.okular

Capability: archive-manager
Resolves-To: org.gnome.FileRoller | org.kde.ark

Capability: password-manager
Resolves-To: org.keepassxc.KeePassXC | app.authpass.AuthPass
